    "title": "Adaptation to Climate Change: Evidence from US Agriculture",
    "summary": "This study examines whether US farmers have adapted to long-term climate change by comparing long-run yield responses to temperature and precipitation trends against short-run panel estimates. The authors find that agricultural productivity for corn and soy is highly sensitive to extreme heat and that farmers have shown little evidence of long-term adaptation, suggesting significant potential losses under future climate scenarios.",
